# Line-ending policy for this project's .context_ledger/ directory.
#
# Installed by 'context-sync bootstrap'. The vendored core under core/ is
# integrity-checked byte-for-byte against core/MANIFEST.sha256 (LF-computed).
# On Windows with core.autocrlf=true, a CRLF checkout makes every hash
# mismatch and kills the sh manifest parser on '\r'-suffixed filenames
# (B-2026-08-30-17). Forcing eol=lf keeps the working tree byte-identical to
# the manifest on every platform. Collaboration event files are parsed line by
# line by the sh helpers, so they must stay LF too.
#
# Paths are relative to this .context_ledger/ directory.

# The vendored core: LF, always. Integrity depends on it.
core/**              text eol=lf
core/MANIFEST.sha256 text eol=lf
core/bin/*           text eol=lf

# Project-owned memory: markdown + configs the sh helpers parse.
memory/**            text eol=lf

# Scripts and structured text anywhere under .context_ledger/.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf

# Binary assets under memory/ (e.g. smoke-test screenshots) must NOT be
# eol-normalised: `memory/** text eol=lf` above is too broad, and the PNG
# signature itself contains a CR-LF pair, so normalisation corrupts the file
# and leaves it permanently "modified" (which also blocks rebases). These come
# last so they win over `memory/**` for these extensions. NOTE: the vendored
# template (core/templates/.gitattributes) has the same over-broad rule — flag
# upstream so a fresh bootstrap doesn't reintroduce it.
memory/**/*.png  binary
memory/**/*.jpg  binary
memory/**/*.jpeg binary
memory/**/*.gif  binary
memory/**/*.webp binary
memory/**/*.ico  binary
memory/**/*.pdf  binary
